### Module(s)

mini.completion

### Neovim version

0.11.x

### Description

Hello, me again o.o)/

According to [`:help popupmenu-keys`](https://neovim.io/doc/user/insert.html#popupmenu-keys):

> Any non-special character:
> - Stop completion without changing the match and insert the typed character.
>
> ...
>
> `<Space>` or `<Tab>`:
> - Stop completion without changing the match and insert the typed character.

So, when I intentionally discard a completion, it should not expand the snippet and insert the typed character instead. But, as the following video shows, mini.completion seems to expand the snippet anyway:

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3f4881a6-47f2-4523-a39b-53952f3901ce

I recorded some logs (included in the later section). After digging it a bit further, I found a solution based on `v:event.reason='discard'`. This was introduced in neovim/neovim#32600, which you authored—awesome! Here’s the [link](https://github.com/loichyan/mini.nvim/commit/3a7f216f5b4513bd5b9cb38c7d63c049fe63c786) to my patch. With this patch, following the same steps as in the above video will only trigger the snippet expansion when `<C-y>` is pressed.

btw, for why this should be considered a bug: when using the function itself as a value, I only need completion for the function name. However, each time I select a function and then press `<Space>`, mini.completion expands the entire snippet, which can bother a lot @.@

### Reproduction

The minimal reproducing configuration:

<details>

```lua
require('mini.completion').setup()
vim.o.signcolumn = 'yes'

-- Copied from: https://github.com/neovim/nvim-lspconfig/blob/45ff1914044de7dbd4cd85053dc09f47312a2f4d/lsp/lua_ls.lua#L70
vim.lsp.config('lua_ls', {
  cmd = { 'lua-language-server' },
  filetypes = { 'lua' },
  root_markers = {
    '.luarc.json',
    '.luarc.jsonc',
    '.luacheckrc',
    '.stylua.toml',
    'stylua.toml',
    'selene.toml',
    'selene.yml',
    '.git',
  },
  settings = {
    Lua = {
      completion = { callSnippet = 'Replace' },
    },
  },
})
vim.lsp.enable('lua_ls')

-- Track logs
_G.log = {}
_G.save_logs = function()
  local f = io.open('nvim-repro/logs.txt', 'w')
  f:write(vim.inspect(log))
  f:close()
  vim.cmd.edit('nvim-repro/logs.txt')
end
vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'CompleteDone', 'CompleteDonePre' }, {
  callback = function(ev)
    table.insert(log, {
      event = ev.event,
      ['v:event'] = vim.v.event,
      ['v:completed_item'] = vim.v.completed_item,
    })
  end,
})
```

</details>

